# Files that must arrive byte-for-byte in a fresh clone.
#
# git detects most binaries by content and leaves them alone, and every PNG in
# screenshots/ is handled that way. A PDF is not: the one-page file
# scripts/make-assets-15.mjs writes is almost all ASCII, so git decided it was
# text and warned that it would convert LF to CRLF on checkout. That conversion
# would add a byte per line and leave every offset in the PDF's xref table
# pointing at the wrong place - a file that is committed intact and broken on
# arrival.
#
# The screenshots are listed as well. They are content-hashed and their URLs are
# pinned to a commit, so a checkout that altered a single byte would serve an
# image whose name no longer matches its contents.

*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.webp binary
